==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Artist Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ramen Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Use Rocker Cat as an extra-durable meatshield to protect your other Cats, especially against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemies. He doesn't work too differently compared to [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], but he trades cost and spammability for a specialization against a trait and the potential to reach much higher health values. Note that he still won't last long against high DPS enemies, which are prominent among melee Angels.

His fast attacks and strong DPS are the icing on the cake, making him effective at clearing annoying peons or to tank, stall and defeat long-ranged area attackers such as [[Master A.]], [[Camelle]] and [[Sunfish Jones]]. Rocker Cat's fast attack rate allows him to also defeat weak [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]] such as [[Metal Hippoe]], [[Metal Doge]] and [[Croconator]] in a reasonable amount of time. His attack cycle does have one significant downside though: Rocker Cat is prone to knocking enemies away from the attacks of stronger units, thereby hindering overall damage output.

With enough upgrades and Research [[Cat Combo|Combo]]s such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], Rocker Cat can be a very valuable meatshield even in stages with little to no Angels. Prominent examples include [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]] and [[Tiny Chopper (Deadly)|Tiny Chopper]], where a sufficiently boosted Rocker Cat can stay alive long enough to permanently stall [[Manic Mohawk Cat (Enemy)|Manic Mohawk]] and Master A., or keep [[Li'l Dark Cat (Enemy)|Li'l Dark Cat]] and [[Sunfish Jones]] pinned forever.

==='''True Form'''===
A high-priority True Form, Ramen Cat gets a notable health increase and a small damage boost, making him even better at what he's already good at. Although the damage boost allows him to chip bosses quicker, it does amplify his tendency to trigger unwanted knockbacks. After a certain point of progression, the issue gets less relevant as enemies' stats get more and more inflated.

==='''Talents'''===
Ramen Cat relies a lot on his basic stats, so Attack Buff, and more importantly, HP Buff are good Talents to invest in. Knockback Resistance drastically improves Ramen Cat's effectiveness against [[Angelic Sleipnir]], stages with [[Mr. Mole]] or [[Trolly Blogger]]s and in other situations. It is somewhat situational, but worth investing in regardless. Resist Slow is not as useful, as Ramen Cat is already rather slow and there are very few enemies that pose a threat to him through the slow effect. Resist Curse, mainly comes into play in mid-game stages that combine [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] and Angel enemies such as [[Rutsborg Vortex]], or Angels and the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]. In this, its function is quite useful with the sheer number of Relic/Angel stages in the mid- to endgame, letting him take a few extra blows from most target traits in said stages for a pretty cheap cost.

==='''Orb'''===
Resistance to Angels is the best, followed by Defense Up. For Ability Orbs, a Cashback Orb is recommended for optimal general meatshielding, though a good Resistance to Angel Orb will sometimes be preferred in type related matchups. As a generalist meatshield, Ramen Cat would benefit from a Dodge Orb, although to a lesser extent than other options.

